{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"S2 PS4 (Gerrit 1843): applied 2 of 5 PS3 advisories — guarded _LazyDataCenterClient.__getattr__ against dunder/probe access (was triggering premature client construction + fail-closed PAT raise), and strengthened the three fail-closed tests from 'exc.type is not AssertionError' to the exact typed errors (ConfigError for unknown backend at compose; BackendEnvError for empty-project and missing-auth at build). Filed follow-ups 2048 (comment_max_chars/jira_cli_timeout capture-not-threaded) and 4698 (Cloud/DC fail-closed symmetry + scope-vs-ambient readiness parity) — both discovered_from e042, deferred as deliberate design decisions. Rebased via fixup+autosquash: S2=b018a3b3bd, S4=0bd33e8840 (replayed), Change-Ids preserved. Full oracle 32/32, lint+typecheck+complexity clean. Pushed stack: S2 PS4 + S4 PS2, gates re-running. S6 (6f14) review-plan BLOCKED twice on IaC citation accuracy (my remediation wrongly located the SSM grant in opcert.tf; it is the shared /rebar/prod/* instance-role policy rebar-gerrit-ssm-params-read in iam.tf, co-used by origin-guard/gerrit secrets and not droppable) — corrected Step5/AC5 to decouple at the application-runtime boundary only; re-reviewing."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787027079632646001,"uuid":"6d137936-d64f-46dd-8cff-14c4cfe6be59"}